    "conclusion": "Event-risk budgeting HURTS portfolio performance. Best event strategy (S3_FOMC_Only): Sharpe=0.8073 vs BH 50/50 Sharpe=0.8814 (dSharpe=-0.0741). No event strategy improves MDD \u2014 all make it worse (S3_FOMC_Only MDD: -33.19% vs S0: -32.49%). 12/VIX smooth strategy dominates all event strategies (Sharpe=0.8438). Confirms K513: event days have POSITIVE mean return (0.111% vs 0.038%) \u2014 reducing exposure forfeits upside. VIX-conditional (S4) reduces false positives but still does not beat baseline. DM test: baseline is significantly BETTER than all event strategies (neg_return t < -3.0). Cross-OOS: S1/S2/S3 lose 5/5 periods, S4 wins 3/5 but still underperforms full-sample. Verdict: Event-risk budgeter is NOT recommended. Smooth continuous strategies (12/VIX, risk parity) >> binary event switching."
